From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:51:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] virtio-gpu: copy only the damage owed to each frame buffer

RESOURCE_FLUSH copied the whole scanout (every row, full width) into the
display frame, so a cursor-sized flush still memcpy'd the entire 4 MB
surface, 60 times a second.

The display backend rotates through several frame buffers, so copying only
the current flush's damage rect would leave stale regions: the guest changed
the resource over the flushed rect, and that change is in no buffer until one
is written. Track the damage per frame buffer instead: a flush puts the
flushed rect onto every buffer (the one it lands in included, since that one
is stale over it too), and a buffer is written when it receives everything it
owes, so only the union of the rects since it was last written is copied.
Fall back to a full copy when the rect is unknown, when a buffer is written
for the first time, and after a reconfigure or disable (the buffers are new,
so nothing may be carried over). The table is keyed per scanout, because
`frame_id` is (each scanout numbers its buffers from 0).
copy_blob_rows now copies a rectangle at its own pixel offset rather than
the whole scanout, and read_2d_resource transfers the same rectangle so
both scanout kinds present only what changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
